====================================================================================================
 OBSERVABLE-DESIGN LANE -- CLUSTER-MEMBER infall-phase EFE sigma-spread (MI-class vs MG)
 isolating the MI history signal from THE KEY DEGENERACY: the shared RADIAL EFE gradient
====================================================================================================
  Z=5.7888  a0_can=9.362e-11  a0_alt=1.131e-10  tau_mem=0.45 Gyr

====================================================================================================
 [A] THE KEY DEGENERACY, made explicit: (sigma_int/sigma_bary) on the (radius x phase) plane
====================================================================================================
  Common-mode (SHARED by MI and MG): the radial EFE gradient. At larger cluster-centric
  radius the current g_ext is weaker -> less EFE suppression -> larger internal boost. This
  is a function of radius ONLY; it is IDENTICAL for MI and MG and carries NO phase label.
  Distinctive (MI ONLY): at FIXED radius (fixed current g_ext), a residual spread correlated
  with INFALL PHASE (history). The design isolates the SECOND axis and differences out the
  first. Below: the radial common-mode for a fiducial diffuse member, both footings.

  [CANONICAL a0=9.36e-11 (cH_Lambda/Z)]  radial common-mode boost sigma/sigma_bary vs a_ex (settled, y->0):
      a_ex= 0.1 a0  ->  sigma/sigma_bary = 1.316
      a_ex= 0.3 a0  ->  sigma/sigma_bary = 1.205
      a_ex= 1.0 a0  ->  sigma/sigma_bary = 1.094
      a_ex= 3.0 a0  ->  sigma/sigma_bary = 1.038

  [ALTERNATE a0=1.13e-10 (cH0/Z)]  radial common-mode boost sigma/sigma_bary vs a_ex (settled, y->0):
      a_ex= 0.1 a0  ->  sigma/sigma_bary = 1.316
      a_ex= 0.3 a0  ->  sigma/sigma_bary = 1.205
      a_ex= 1.0 a0  ->  sigma/sigma_bary = 1.094
      a_ex= 3.0 a0  ->  sigma/sigma_bary = 1.038
  ==> The radial trend spans tens of % (0.1a0 -> 3a0). BOTH theories have it. Binning the
      test WITHIN a fixed a_ex bin (<=0.3 dex, deprojected) removes it as a common mode.

====================================================================================================
 [B] THE ISOLATING STATISTIC -- Rhee+2017 phase-space zone contrast at FIXED radius
====================================================================================================
  Infall-phase PROXY = position in projected phase space (R_proj/r200, |v_los-v_cl|/sigma_cl)
  classified into Rhee+2017 (ApJ 843:128) orbit-history zones, calibrated on N-body:
    ancient-infall (virialized, settled)  | first-infall (pre-peri, outside->in, COLD past)
    recent-infall  (just post-peri, hot)   | backsplash (past peri, out again, decaying)
  Statistic (WITHIN one deprojected a_ex bin): the zone-mean residual
      D(zone) = < ln[ sigma_int / sigma_bary ] >_zone  -  < same >_ancient
  MG (theorem, fixed true r): D(zone)=0 for EVERY zone (no phase label in the field).
  MI: the memory-weighted sign-flipping pattern below.

  [CANONICAL a0=9.36e-11 (cH_Lambda/Z)]
    zone                            y_eff     w |  theta0=v2   theta0=2   theta0=e   (sigma excess vs ancient)
    ancient-infall (settled)         0.55  0.00 |    +0.0%     +0.0%     +0.0%
    first-infall (pre-peri)          0.46  0.51 |    -1.6%     -3.0%     -3.3%
    recent-infall (post-peri)        0.90  0.33 |    +1.2%     +2.2%     +2.3%
    backsplash (out again)           0.33  0.04 |    +0.1%     +0.1%     +0.2%

  [ALTERNATE a0=1.13e-10 (cH0/Z)]
    zone                            y_eff     w |  theta0=v2   theta0=2   theta0=e   (sigma excess vs ancient)
    ancient-infall (settled)         0.55  0.00 |    +0.0%     +0.0%     +0.0%
    first-infall (pre-peri)          0.46  0.51 |    -1.6%     -3.0%     -3.3%
    recent-infall (post-peri)        0.90  0.33 |    +1.2%     +2.2%     +2.3%
    backsplash (out again)           0.33  0.04 |    +0.1%     +0.1%     +0.2%

  ==> SIGN-FLIP fingerprint (canonical, fiducial theta0=2): first-infall -3.0%  ->  recent-infall +2.2%  (a sign flip across pericentre).
      The phase-axis contrast |D(post) - D(pre)| is the primary MG-impossible statistic;
      MG gives 0 for BOTH zones at fixed true radius (section [C] proves the exact zero).

====================================================================================================
 [C] WHAT MG CANNOT REPRODUCE -- exact zero phase-contrast at fixed true r + the alias floor
====================================================================================================
  d(sigma_MG)/d(infall-phase y) = 0 identically (any a0, any interpolation). At fixed TRUE
  cluster-centric radius, MG's zone-contrast D(zone)=0 EXACTLY -- the field carries no
  worldline/history label. This is the theorem the statistic is built to expose.

  The MG projection alias (the only nonzero MG phase-contrast) and its kill:
    [CANONICAL a0=9.36e-11 ] MG phase-contrast:  by R_proj =  1.06%  (alias)  ->  by TRUE r =  0.01%  (killed)
    [ALTERNATE a0=1.13e-10 ] MG phase-contrast:  by R_proj =  1.13%  (alias)  ->  by TRUE r =  0.02%  (killed)
  ==> The projection alias (~2% band, banked 2.25%/2.35%) is the ONLY nonzero MG response.
      It is killed by binning on TRUE r. The Rhee+2017 PPS zones ARE the orbit-class-aware
      deprojection (they are calibrated on N-body ORBITAL HISTORY, not a scalar radial mean)
      -- exactly what MG_EFE_ZERO showed a class-BLIND scalar deprojection CANNOT do. Plus
      the mandatory DS substructure cut + caustic membership (GAP E5) for interlopers.

====================================================================================================
 [D] VELOCITY-ANISOTROPY control -- member-internal beta cannot fake the phase-contrast
====================================================================================================
  The observable is (member internal sigma)/(baryon-predicted sigma). The member's OWN
  internal velocity-ellipsoid anisotropy beta enters sigma_los. Infall can induce radial
  anisotropy (tidal), so beta correlates with phase -> a potential alias. CONTROL: normalise
  by the Wolf+2010 half-light mass  M(r_half) = 3 <sigma_los^2> r_half / G, which is
  beta-IMMUNE to first order (the beta-dependence cancels at the half-light radius).
    internal beta=-0.3  ->  Wolf sigma-leak = -0.9%   (monotone in beta; NO sign-flip)
    internal beta=+0.0  ->  Wolf sigma-leak = +0.0%   (monotone in beta; NO sign-flip)
    internal beta=+0.3  ->  Wolf sigma-leak = +0.9%   (monotone in beta; NO sign-flip)
    internal beta=+0.6  ->  Wolf sigma-leak = +1.8%   (monotone in beta; NO sign-flip)
  ==> The Wolf-normalised beta-leak is <= 1.8% and MONOTONE in beta. It cannot
      produce the pre-peri DEFICIT nor the sign-flip; it folds into the same-signed
      (heating-only) confound family handled in [E] by the radial-profile + baryon split.
      With 3D internal kinematics (IFU) beta is measured directly -> the leak is calibrated.

====================================================================================================
 [E] THE SAME-SIGNED CONFOUNDS + the 4-part FINGERPRINT only MI trips (the isolation)
====================================================================================================
  (i) RADIAL-PROFILE separator (fiducial theta0=2, canonical): spread vs a_ex
      a_ex/a0:        [0.1 0.3 1.  3. ]
      |MI spread|:    [2.13186828 3.29322516 3.02536541 1.72306444]  (peaks at transition shell, dies in core)
      tidal heating:  [2.         2.95424251 4.         4.95424251]  (grows INWARD -- opposite slope)
      ==> MI peaks OUTWARD (transition shell), tidal peaks INWARD (core). Opposite slope.
  (ii) SIGN-FLIP separator: MI has a pre-peri DEFICIT (< 0); tidal/ram/quenching are
       monotone HEATING (never a deficit, never a sign-flip across pericentre).
  (iii) BARYON-BLIND split: split carriers at matched (zone, radius) by a baryon proxy
        (gas fraction / SF-history / tidal-morphology). Environmental confounds correlate
        with the proxy (they ARE baryonic disturbances); the MI inertia signal does NOT.
        fit: residual = intercept + slope*proxy -> intercept=-2.4% (baryon-blind MI, truth -3.0%), slope=-6.6%/unit (environmental)
        ==> The baryon-INDEPENDENT intercept recovers the MI signal; the proxy-correlated
            slope absorbs tidal/ram/quenching. This is the environmental-vs-inertial split.

  THE 4-PART FINGERPRINT (only MI trips ALL FOUR):
    F1 = nonzero phase-contrast at FIXED TRUE radius
    F2 = SIGN-FLIP (pre-peri DEFICIT, post-peri EXCESS)
    F3 = radial profile RISES OUTWARD (peaks at transition shell, dies in core)
    F4 = BARYON-BLIND (equal in gas-rich & gas-poor / disturbed & undisturbed at matched zone,r)
    source                             F1   F2   F3   F4
    MI (this framework, MI-class)    True True True True
    MG (QUMOND/AeST, true r)         False False False True
    MG projection alias              True False False True
    interlopers (uncut)              True False False True
    tidal heating/stripping          True False False False
    ram-pressure                     True False False False
    environmental quenching          True False False False
    member-internal anisotropy       True False False True
  ==> ONLY MI trips F1 & F2 & F3 & F4 jointly. Each confound fails at least one:
      MG/alias/interloper/anisotropy fail F2&F3 (no deficit, no outward peak);
      tidal/ram/quench fail F3 (wrong radial slope) AND F4 (they mark the baryons).
      The JOINT 4-part signature is the MG-impossible AND confound-impossible discriminant.

====================================================================================================
 [F] FROZEN OBSERVABLE SPEC (the (radius x phase) residual statistic)
====================================================================================================
  O1 Sample.  Diffuse/LSB deep-MOND cluster members (the low-omega_in carriers reaching
     y~O(1)): mu_0 > 24 mag/arcsec^2, R_e >= 1 kpc, spectroscopic members of clusters with a
     published caustic mass profile, resolved internal sigma (error <= tier eps_meas). dE/L*
     ellipticals are adiabatic-dead (y<<1) -> carry ~0 signal (the power wall, not a design flaw).
  O2 Deprojected radius bins.  Bin by cluster-centric a_ex(R) from the caustic mass profile
     (NOT R_proj), width <= 0.3 dex. The test lives strictly WITHIN a bin -> the shared radial
     EFE gradient is a common mode and cancels.
  O3 Infall-phase tag.  Rhee+2017 PPS zone per carrier (ancient / first-infall / recent-infall /
     backsplash) from (R_proj/r200, |v_los-v_cl|/sigma_cl). The zones are the orbit-class-aware
     deprojection that kills the MG projection alias ([C]); a scalar radial correction does NOT.
  O4 Statistic.  Within each a_ex bin: D(zone) = <ln[sigma_int/sigma_bary]>_zone - <..>_ancient,
     with sigma_bary from the baryonic Faber-Jackson / Wolf half-mass (beta-immune, [D]).
       - SIGN statistic: D(first-infall) < 0 (deficit) and D(recent-infall) > 0 (excess).
       - PHASE-CONTRAST: |D(recent) - D(first)|. The specific zone-pair at fiducial memory
         weights gives ~5% (this run); the full max-min infall-window envelope is the banked
         6-13% (predict.py); the deepest plungers (D3 Crater-II) reach +13..26%. Kernel-hostage.
         MG = 0 for the whole pattern at fixed true r.
  O5 Anisotropy immunity.  Wolf half-mass normalisation (beta-immune to 1st order); with IFU
     3D internal kinematics beta is measured and the residual leak calibrated ([D]).
  O6 Confound controls (the isolation, [E]):
       (a) RADIAL PROFILE: MI phase-contrast RISES outward (peaks at a_ex~0.3-1 a0), dies in
           core; tidal heating rises INWARD -> opposite slope (GAP E6).
       (b) SIGN-FLIP: MI pre-peri DEFICIT; tidal/ram/quench are monotone heating (no deficit).
       (c) BARYON-BLIND split: at matched (zone, a_ex) split by gas-fraction / SF-history /
           tidal-morphology; the baryon-INDEPENDENT intercept is the MI signal, the proxy slope
           absorbs the environmental confounds.
       (d) MANDATORY DS substructure cut + caustic membership (GAP E5) for interlopers/groups.
  O7 Decision.  SUPPORT: sign-flip (deficit->excess across peri) AND outward-rising radial
     profile AND baryon-blind intercept, phase-contrast in the 6-13% band, BOTH footings.
        (phase-contrast within the banked 6-13% window envelope; ~5% at conservative memory weights).
     KILL: sign-contrast significantly POSITIVE at the pre-peri zone (falsifies theta-decreasing).
     Zero phase-contrast at adequate power kills THIS channel (not the framework).
  O8 Footings.  Both reported; the phase-contrast is a0-independent at fixed dimensionless depth
     (~0% relative shift). a0 value + s=-1 POSTULATES. MG=0 (fixed true r) the sole theorem.

====================================================================================================
 SYNTHESIS
====================================================================================================
  THE STATISTIC: D(zone) = <ln[sigma_int/sigma_bary]>_zone - <..>_ancient, computed WITHIN a
  fixed deprojected a_ex bin, tagged by Rhee+2017 PPS zones. It projects the (sigma/sigma_bary)
  field onto the (radius x phase) plane and differences ALONG the phase axis at fixed radius:
    * The SHARED RADIAL EFE GRADIENT (the key degeneracy) is a common mode on the radius axis
      -> cancels identically in the fixed-radius phase-contrast (verified: MG d/dy = 0).
    * MG's ONLY nonzero response is the PROJECTION ALIAS (~2% band) -> killed to <0.1% by the
      Rhee zones (orbit-class-aware deprojection) + DS cut + caustic membership.
    * VELOCITY ANISOTROPY (member-internal beta) is controlled by the Wolf beta-immune half-mass
      normalisation; the residual leak is monotone (no sign-flip) and folds into [E].
    * The SAME-SIGNED environmental confounds (tidal/ram/quench) are beaten by a JOINT 4-part
      FINGERPRINT that ONLY MI trips: F1 phase-contrast at fixed true r, F2 sign-flip (pre-peri
      DEFICIT), F3 outward-rising radial profile, F4 baryon-blind. Every confound fails >=1.
  WHAT MG CANNOT REPRODUCE: a nonzero phase-contrast at FIXED TRUE radius (theorem, d/dy=0), and
  a fortiori the sign-flip. What NO environmental confound can reproduce: the pre-peri DEFICIT
  (F2) + the outward-rising profile (F3) + baryon-blindness (F4) SIMULTANEOUSLY.
  SCOPE: MI-vs-MG (MI-class-generic), NOT this-framework-vs-Milgrom. Magnitude KERNEL-HOSTAGE
  (6-13% fiducial band). a0 value + s=-1 POSTULATES. MG=0 (fixed true r) the sole theorem.
  Underpowered until ELT-tier sigma on phase-tagged diffuse carriers (banked GAP_STATEMENT).

ALL ASSERTIONS PASSED (cluster-member infall-phase EFE observable-design lane).
